<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/calculator-paperwork.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal-services/">Services</a></li><li aria-current="page">Carrier Estimate Review</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Carrier Estimate Review for Washington Property Claims</h1><p class="lede">Before anyone demands appraisal, it helps to know exactly where the insurer’s estimate falls short and what that gap is worth. A review gives you that answer.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Output</dt><dd>Written gap summary</dd></div><div><dt>Turnaround</dt><dd>Days, not weeks</dd></div><div><dt>Next step</dt><dd>Supplement or appraisal</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>What a review looks at</h2>
<p>An insurer’s estimate can run dozens of pages, with codes and abbreviations that are hard to follow. We go through it line by line and compare it with the damage, your photos and any contractor estimate you have.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Scope.</strong> Are all damaged rooms, slopes, elevations and structures included?</li>
<li><strong>Quantities.</strong> Do the square footage, linear feet and roof squares match the measurements?</li>
<li><strong>Pricing.</strong> Are unit prices realistic for your county and the current market?</li>
<li><strong>Depreciation.</strong> Is it reasonable for the age and condition of each item, and applied only where the policy allows?</li>
<li><strong>Overhead and profit.</strong> Is a general contractor reasonably needed to coordinate the trades?</li>
<li><strong>Code items.</strong> Has ordinance or law coverage been considered where required?</li>
</ul>
<h2>What you get</h2>
<p>A plain-English summary of the gaps, with the approximate dollar value of each, and our honest view of the best next step. Often that’s a documented supplement request to the insurer. Sometimes it’s appraisal. Occasionally it’s a conversation with an attorney or the Office of the Insurance Commissioner.</p>
<h2>Why review first</h2>
<p>Demanding appraisal without knowing your number is a gamble. A review shows whether the gap is large enough to justify appraisal costs, and it gives your appraiser a head start if you go forward.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I need my own contractor estimate for a review?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It helps, but it isn’t required. We can review the carrier’s estimate against photos and our own inspection.</p></div></details><details><summary>Will you contact my insurer?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Not during a review unless you ask us to. The review is for you to decide what to do next.</p></div></details><details><summary>What does a review cost?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>We quote a flat fee in writing based on the size of the claim before starting. The first conversation is free.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="cards3 tight"><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/neutral-umpire-services/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-review.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-review-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork-review.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Neutral Umpire Services</h3><span class="pcard-p">Impartial umpire for appraisal panels when the two appraisers can’t agree on the amount of loss.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-table-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation-table.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Appraisal Clause Representation</h3><span class="pcard-p">We act as the appraiser you name once either side demands appraisal under your policy.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/home-insurance-claim-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/home-evergreens.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/home-evergreens-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/home-evergreens.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Single-family houses, townhomes and condo units where the carrier’s estimate misses real repair costs.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width